}}, {"id": ["mesh:D005234"], "is_neural_normalized": false, "mention": "hepatic steatosis", "obj": "disease", "prob": 0.9999958276748657, "span": {"begin": 1036, "end": 1053}}, {"id": ["NCBIGene:196"], "is_neural_normalized": false, "mention": "AhR", "obj": "gene", "prob": 0.9976668357849121, "span": {"begin": 1063, "end": 1066}}, {"id": ["NCBIGene:196"], "is_neural_normalized": true, "mention": "hepatic AhR", "obj": "gene", "prob": 0.8706589937210083, "span": {"begin": 1244, "end": 1255}}, {"id": ["mesh:D005227"], "is_neural_normalized": false, "mention": "fatty-acid", "obj": "drug", "prob": 0.9927621483802795, "span": {"begin": 1297, "end": 1307}}, {"id": ["mesh:D005234"], "is_neural_normalized": true, "mention": "hepatic lipid", "obj": "disease", "prob": 0.8090639114379883, "span": {"begin": 1355, "end": 1368}}], "text": "Activation of AhR can directly alter hepatic lipid homeostasis through several mechanistically interconnected processes. In mice, constitutive hepatic AhR activation induces spontaneous triglyceride accumulation and steatosis, associated with increased expression of the fatty-acid transporter CD36 and other fatty-acid transport proteins, decreased fatty-acid oxidation, reduced hepatic triglyceride export and increased oxidative stress. CD36 has been identified as a direct transcriptional target of AhR, and deletion of CD36 markedly attenuates the steatotic effect of AhR agonism, providing experimental support for a causal AhR&ndash;lipid accumulation relationship (PMID: 20303349)  Additional loss-of-function evidence supports this relationship. AhR-deficient mice are protected against high-fat-diet-induced hepatic steatosis, and display altered expression of genes involved in fatty-acid uptake and lipid metabolism. In another experimental model, activation of the AhR&ndash;CD36 axis increased hepatocyte lipid uptake and hepatic steatosis, whereas AhR knockdown or pharmacological antagonism reduced lipid accumulation (PMID: 25907315)  Taken together, these findings provide a biologically plausible mechanism whereby sustained hepatic AhR activation can shift the balance between fatty-acid uptake, synthesis, oxidation and export toward hepatic lipid accumulation.", "timestamp": "Tue Oct 13 15:57:52 +0000 2026"}